cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "entities-images: local-first build infrastructure for the fabric Godot fork"
abstract: >
  Builds of the multiplayer-fabric Godot engine fork: player export templates and
  editor binaries, cross-compiled from Linux to every supported platform and built
  natively where that is simpler. There is deliberately no CI workflow -- every
  output is produced by running a just recipe on a developer machine, which is the
  same rule the workspace states about where a thing is built: CI is the overflow,
  not the first attempt, and a cold runner rebuilds what an incremental local build
  already has.
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
    email: ernest.lee@chibifire.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4570-1436"
version: 0.1.0-dev.1
date-released: "2026-08-17"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric/entities-images"
keywords:
  - godot
  - cross-compilation
  - build-infrastructure
  - reproducible-builds
references:

  - type: software
    title: "entities-godot: the multiplayer-fabric Godot fork"
    url: "https://github.com/v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric/entities-godot"
    notes: >
      The engine every output here is a build of. The pin lives in docs/DEVELOPMENT.md
      rather than here, so there is one place that says which commit shipped.

  - type: software
    title: "just: a command runner"
    authors:
      - family-names: Rodarmor
        given-names: Casey
    url: "https://github.com/casey/just"
    notes: >
      Every artefact this repository produces is a just recipe. It is the build system,
      not a convenience wrapper over one.

  - type: software
    title: "SCons"
    url: "https://scons.org/"
    notes: "Godot's own build system, which the recipes invoke rather than replace."
